# Jak 3, 0.1.8 (LIST-0.1.8 item 5, Hold the gun while driving; build 103: the drawn gun stays Jak's, not Daxter's as the
# game's seated poses give it). Run with JAKVR_TEST_CONTINUE=hanga-start JAKVR_TEST_GUN=1 QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000
# JAKVR_STATE_TRACE=1 JAKVR_BODY_TRACE=1: the glider (its flag 32 keeps his gun), the continue seating him in it.
# The opening skipped and a new game started as jak3_ride_wheel.sim does; once seated, the right hand over the right
# shoulder and its grip squeezed there (the shoulder's holster draws in a vehicle), brought ahead and let go (the gun
# stays drawn), a shot (R1), then the gun put away over the shoulder (squeezed and let go there). Expect "[vr-pad] Hold
# the gun while driving: this vehicle keeps his gun ...", "[vr-holster] Hold the gun while driving: the drawn gun is in
# his hand (not Daxter's)", "[vr-body] ... gun bones 36 (of its 36) in hand 1" while it is drawn, and the gun in the
# right hand in the pictures.
# The lines from 10000 count from the frame the continue seats him (QUEST_SIM_ALIGN=10000; pc-vr.gc
# vr-test-continue!, "[vr] test: seated by the continue, the set-up done", build 104 on), the gun 60 frames after it.
# (Sims rg3 and rg3b, builds 103 and 104: the hijacked pickup's continue, ctyport-hijack-decoy, loads the city but
# leaves Jak on foot at the port, so the pickup is a headset check, HEADSET_CHECKLIST.md.)
